<title>GERMANY: German jobs chief cannot rule out 4.5 mln jobless.</title>
<headline>German jobs chief cannot rule out 4.5 mln jobless.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bernhard Jagoda, chief of the German Federal Labour Office, said on Thursday he could not rule out German unemployment on an unadjusted basis rising to 4.5 million in the coming months.</p>
<p>&quot;If we have 4.148 million jobless in December and we have such bad weather in January, and if this continues until March, I cannot rule out (unadjusted) figures hitting 4.5 million,&quot; Jagoda told a news conference.</p>
<p>The Federal Labour Office earlier announced a rise of 48,000 in unemployment across Germany on an adjusted basis.</p>
</text>
